<section id="worth" style={{ padding: "1rem 1rem 2.5rem", background: "var(--bg-secondary)" }}>
  <div class="container" style={{ maxWidth: "1000px" }}>
    <span class="section-title">Value check</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Are Udemy Microsoft vouchers worth it in 2026?</h2>
    <p style={{ color: "var(--muted)", fontSize: "0.95rem", lineHeight: 1.75, maxWidth: "840px", margin: "0.75rem 0 1.5rem" }}>
      It depends on which exam you need. For a current Fundamentals or Associate exam, the 10% saving is real and the convenience is high. For a replacement code that Udemy has not listed yet, direct with Microsoft is the only option.
    </p>
    <div class="choice-grid">
      <div class="choice-card">
        <h3>Voucher-only wins when…</h3>
        <p>You need a current exam, the live price is below Microsoft's list fee, and you are already scoring above 85% on timed practice exams. Pair it with a discounted prep course and keep the total under the cost of a direct exam plus full-price training.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="choice-card">
        <h3>Retake Assurance wins when…</h3>
        <p>You are attempting a $165 Associate or Expert exam where a second full fee is painful, or it is your first role-based exam and a failed attempt would derail your timeline. Check that the exam page actually offers it before relying on it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="choice-card">
        <h3>Direct with Microsoft wins when…</h3>
        <p>You need a replacement exam — AI-901, AI-103, AI-300, AI-200, SC-500, AZ-802, AB-410 or AB-650 — because Udemy has not listed a voucher for those codes yet. Direct is also better if you need local-currency pricing or maximum date flexibility.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="choice-card">
        <h3>Other legitimate ways to pay less</h3>
        <p>Employer or academic bulk vouchers, Microsoft Learn challenges and event vouchers, and coupon-discounted prep courses. Coupons work on courses, never on the voucher itself. Microsoft's official learning paths and practice assessments are free.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style={{ color: "var(--muted)", fontSize: "0.9rem", lineHeight: 1.75, margin: "1.25rem 0 0" }}>
      For the broader coupon strategy, see the <a href="/udemy-coupons-guide" style={{ color: "var(--brand)", fontWeight: 600 }}>Udemy coupons guide</a> and the step-by-step <a href="/how-to-redeem-coupon" style={{ color: "var(--brand)", fontWeight: 600 }}>coupon redemption guide</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="study" style={{ padding: "2rem 1rem 2.5rem" }}>
  <div class="container" style={{ maxWidth: "900px" }}>
    <span class="section-title">Before you book</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading">How to prepare so you don't waste the voucher</h2>
    <p style={{ color: "var(--muted)", fontSize: "0.95rem", lineHeight: 1.75, margin: "0.75rem 0 1rem" }}>
      Most candidates need 2–4 weeks for a Fundamentals exam and 8–12 weeks for an Associate or Expert exam. Microsoft exams are scenario-heavy, so course completion alone is not enough: use the official skills outline, hands-on labs in a free tenant or Azure subscription, and two timed practice runs above 85%.
    </p>
    <ul style={{ margin: 0, paddingLeft: "1.2rem", color: "var(--muted)", fontSize: "0.92rem", lineHeight: 1.85 }}>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>Use the official study guide for the current code.</strong> Microsoft publishes the skills measured and weightings for every exam. Study to the code on the voucher, not a retired outline.</li>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>Do the labs.</strong> AZ-104, AZ-400, SC-200 and DP-300 reward hands-on work in Azure, Entra ID, Sentinel, Defender and Azure SQL. Watching videos is not enough.</li>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>Do not book before two clean practice runs.</strong> A voucher is a prepaid attempt, not a diagnostic. Rescheduling is allowed, but the expiry date does not move.</li>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>Check the retirement calendar before booking.</strong> If your exam has a published retirement date, leave enough room to sit it before the cutoff, or study the replacement instead.</li>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>Match the course to the current code.</strong> AI-103, AI-300, AI-200, SC-500 and AZ-802 materials are still catching up. Check the course's last-updated date before buying.</li>
      <li><strong style={{ color: "var(--text)" }}>Plan the renewal.</strong> Fundamentals certifications do not expire; Associate and Expert certifications need a free online renewal each year. Put a calendar reminder in place after you pass.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

